# What is a Function?

A Function is a database object that accepts input parameters and returns exactly one value.

Unlike Stored Procedures, Functions are mainly used for calculations and formatting.

---

# Syntax

```sql
DELIMITER $$

CREATE FUNCTION FunctionName(Parameter Datatype)
RETURNS Datatype

DETERMINISTIC

BEGIN

RETURN value;

END $$

DELIMITER ;
```

---

# Execute Function

```sql
SELECT FunctionName(value);
```

---

# Example 1

Return Square of Number

```sql
DELIMITER $$

CREATE FUNCTION SquareNumber(num INT)

RETURNS INT

DETERMINISTIC

BEGIN

RETURN num * num;

END $$

DELIMITER ;
```

Execute

```sql
SELECT SquareNumber(5);
```

Output

```
25
```

